The tick charges the thread whose turn it is as if it earned the whole processor, so it spends nothing.
A thread never spends its account, however long it runs;
every tick of a turn with time costs the thread a tick less its units.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a tick did not cost the thread whose turn it was a tick less its units

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -369,7 +369,7 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
     wake_stale = true;
     if (turn != NULL) {
         account_refill(turn);
-        turn->balance = account_after(turn->balance, thread_units(turn), ticks);
+        turn->balance = account_after(turn->balance, TICK_PARTS, ticks);
         turn->stamp += ticks;
     }
     sched_ticks += ticks;
